1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:01,171
Quick recap.

2
00:00:01,171 --> 00:00:06,367
Epithelium is packed cells on a basement membrane, with no blood vessels.

3
00:00:06,367 --> 00:00:10,260
Connective tissue is few cells in a lot of matrix.

4
00:00:10,260 --> 00:00:16,562
Tendons are collagen and join muscle to bone; ligaments are elastic and join bone to bone.

5
00:00:16,562 --> 00:00:21,458
Cartilage has no blood supply; mammalian bone has Haversian systems.

6
00:00:21,458 --> 00:00:28,541
Muscle is striated, cardiac or smooth, and in a contracting sarcomere the A band stays the same.

7
00:00:28,541 --> 00:00:37,864
And in a neuron, dendrites bring impulses in, the axon carries them out, myelin makes them jump, and the synapse is one way.

